## Recomputed cjxl-parity status for the 4 OPEN codec_wiki cells

`OPEN if bytes_pct > 3.0 AND (bfly_pct > 3.0 OR ssim2 < -1.0)`

| cell | W134 status | W135 bytes% | W135 bfly% | W135 ssim2 | W135 status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| codec_wiki e5 d=4 | **OPEN** | +26.30% | -8.33% | -0.98 | **FIXED** ← W44-135 hard-target close |
| codec_wiki e6 d=4 | OPEN | +27.32% | +7.82% | -1.03 | OPEN (ssim2 just barely below -1.0) |
| codec_wiki e7 d=4 | OPEN | +42.68% | +7.39% | +0.06 | OPEN (bfly drives) |
| codec_wiki e7 d=6 | OPEN | +43.31% | +3.29% | +5.58 | OPEN (bfly drives) |

Note: codec_wiki e6/e7 d=4 and e7 d=6 STAY OPEN — but they were OPEN at
W44-110 baseline TOO (before W44-124 even existed). The W44-110 row in
the W44-134 memo explicitly tracks these as "STILL OPEN — worsened
under W44-124". W44-135 partially reverts to baseline (W135 SSIM2 better
than W134 by +1.43/+1.22/+0.64 respectively) but doesn't add new closes
on top.

## Zero NEW FIXED→OPEN flips on the harness

- 3 TERMINAL_OPEN cells: byte-identical (auto rejects via m3 gate).
- 2 IMAC_G3_OPEN cells: byte-identical (m3 gate rejects).
- 9 PHOTO cells: byte-identical (ed gate rejects).
- 6 CODEC_WIKI in-band cells: byte-identical (auto fires, preserves
  W44-124 default behaviour).

## Why baseline_off and auto_default came out identical at every cell

Per `api.rs::StrategyOverrides::apply_to` (lines 4196-4202), the
mapping is:

- `dct32_keep_hint: Some(true)`  → `Dct32SearchPolicy::KeepWhenDct64Suppressed`
- `dct32_keep_hint: Some(false)` → `Dct32SearchPolicy::FollowDct64Suppression`
- `dct32_keep_hint: None`        → `FollowDct64Suppression` (default)

Both `Some(false)` and `None` map to `FollowDct64Suppression`, which
the W44-129 Chunk C call site (encoder.rs:3214) consults as
"no caller override → ask env-var + W44-124 + W44-135 auto-discriminator".

`Some(false)` is therefore NOT a "force-off" anymore (it was when the
legacy `with_dct32_keep_hint(Option<bool>)` API existed pre-W44-130.2
Chunk D; that field was deleted). The 3-mode harness in this example
collapses to a 2-mode comparison (auto ≡ baseline_off, vs keep_dct32).
The comparison against the W44-134 ledger numbers IS the real A/B that
validates W44-135.

Follow-on candidate: add a `Dct32SearchPolicy::ForceFollow` (or rename
to ForceSuppress) so callers can truly force-off — useful for paired
A/B benches and for users who want to disable the W44-124 lever.
Tracked as a separate non-blocking issue.

